  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 5$ matrix. If $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
  "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $B$ is formed by $3$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
